{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560396-v20-can-dhampirs-be-also-ghouls","id":1560396,"title":"[V20] Can Dhampirs be also Ghouls?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-06-05T19:51:45-07:00","id":1560396,"title":"[V20] Can Dhampirs be also Ghouls?","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> Puntual question for V20, as the title says: Can Dhampirs be also Ghouls?<br /> <br /> I am confused since the Dhampir section on Becket's Jihad Diary, states on the same page:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Becket's Jihad Diary p.144</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Dhampirs are physical\u00adly the same as Revenants<br /> however</b>, and all but the most knowledgeable<br /> Kindred would assume she is a masterless ghoul.<br /> ...<br /> \u2022 Blood pool: 10. The Dhampir regenerates 1 blood<br /> point per day. <b>She can drink vitae to replenish<br /> more quickly, with all the usual effects</b> (i.e. <b>be\u00ad<br /> coming</b> blood bound or <b>a ghou</b>l).\u200b<br /> ...<br /> \u2022 The Dhampir\u2019s vampiric heritage makes it im\u00ad<br /> possible for her to become a changeling, demon,<br /> mage, mummy, werewolf, or their related kin.<br /> <b>She can be blood bound to a vampire, though<br /> she does not become a ghoul.</b> A Dhampir can<br /> become Imbued, but does not lose their Dham\u00ad<br /> pir template.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>So, can they be or not a Ghoul? I mean mainly for the increasing disciplines capabilities that ghouls/revenants get versus Dhampirs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-05T23:02:53-07:00","id":1560402,"title":"","content":"<br /> Beckett's Jyhad Diary is a strange supplement, because it it primarily an in-universe storybook.<br /> If you look closely several things are either black or red, like the things regarding Dhampirs and for example confriming Inyanga, the Gangrel Primogen of Chicago, is actually a Laibon<br /> I like call in IC lore and OOC lore, something more optional than &quot;set in stone&quot; like for example Vitel is not Vitel.<br /> To prevent game stats from breaking the immersion of the story, the publishers colored the layout of all purely mechanical stat blocks and rule breakdowns in this uniform dark red ink<br /> While the black version is the story-&quot;friendly&quot;, the &quot;if it fits, why not..?&quot;<br /> <br /> So you have in this case an optional approach, &quot;Dhampirs could be ghouled&quot; and the &quot;no, they can not&quot;<br /> <br /> Time of Thin Blood and Sins of the Blood agree with the red text, they can be blood bound to a vampire, but they do not become a ghoul<br /> <br /> Strangely enough, this is something they almost share with the Dhampyrs of the Kuei-jin; the Shade Walkers or Twilight Children are unable to be ghouled and cannot experience the blood bond when tasting Kindred vitae<br /> <br /> So it is<br /> a, I am right, there are two set of rules, one if more &quot;immersion friendly&quot; and one that is a bit more strict and more often than not even backed up by oldelr books<br /> b, I am wrong, it is just a coincidence the red rules are fit in the metaplot and the black is portryed more of an optional, unconfrimed things thus the ghoulling part is simply an error, typo<br /> <br /> (If you want to highlight the difference between Dhampirs and Dhampyrs, the kids of the 15-16 Generation, half-human, half cainites inherits the vulnerability and curse of the vitae and they could be blooded, while the reincarnations of the Jin Hai, the Golden Children, the original offspring of the Wan Xian reborn in a half-cursed body of a Kuei-jin and a human (or hengeyokai) are free from those potential shackles...<br /> ...or go with the rules, and highlight how strangely and curiously similar the two breed are, so maybe the the Cainites are indeed stuck in a quasy chih-mei state (would explain why it is a possibility for a Salubri to awaken their P'o and start their Dharmic journey) )<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 06-06-2026, 04:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}